      "writtenOn": "2019-02-05T23:44:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the case of SimState, the index of the array indicates the slot.\nSo, we simply have: repeated SimState sim_states\n\nThis is not the case here and it means that logic in aggregation will be more complex: now we need to loop thru the list of ActiveSubscriptionInfo and search the item with the correct slot_index.\n\nI personally preferred the previous approach, where carrier_id (a property of the SIM card) was in the same structure as SIM status, so that the two went hand-in-hand, leaving \"is_opportunistic\" out as an additional boolean or structure.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1542,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1542,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c1b07394ab372d85d9bd4801d22d632527d27511",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2352ca5_0cf24663",
        "filename": "proto/src/telephony.proto",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 1542,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098848
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-06T00:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The carrier id and isOpportunistic is a property of Subscription, but not SIM card. This is why I separated them into a different structure. \n\nAlso, other event who care about the carrier_id and other subscription info can benefit from the ActiveSubscriptionInfo, they don\u0027t need to include the sim state in this case.\n\nThe other benefit is that we can save the space when the sim card is absent. If the sim card is absent, we don\u0027t need to upload an invalid subscription_info.",
      "parentUuid": "5db33f3a_5c0296f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1542,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1542,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c1b07394ab372d85d9bd4801d22d632527d27511",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
